  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 1, 'Drink a full glass of water, then decide on the very next small thing, and only that.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 2, 'Write three must-dos for today on a scrap of paper, and give yourself permission to drop everything else.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 3, 'Say quietly to yourself, "This is a hard day, not a hard life," and let it sit for one breath.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 4, 'Eat something small right now, even a handful of crackers or a piece of fruit, before you deal with the next thing.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 5, 'Text one trusted person: "I''m having a rough day, no need to fix it, just wanted someone to know."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 6, 'Step outside your door for two minutes and look at the sky, whatever the weather is doing.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 7, 'Plan only the next hour. Write down what goes in it and leave the rest of the day blank for now.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 8, 'Change into a clean, soft shirt, even if you are staying home and nobody will see it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 9, 'Put on one favorite song and do nothing else for the length of it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 10, 'Pick the task you are dreading most and write down what a "good enough" version of it would look like.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 11, 'Lie down flat on the floor or a bed for five minutes with your eyes closed, phone face down.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 12, 'Breathe out slowly through your mouth three times, longer out than in, before you answer the next message.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 13, 'If today feels unbearable, or you have thoughts of harming yourself, call or text 988 any time, day or night. In an emergency, call 911.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 14, 'Move one thing off today''s list to another day, and tell whoever needs to know in one short sentence.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 15, 'Ask yourself what you would say to a friend having this exact day, then say it to yourself, out loud if you can.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 16, 'Wash your face with cool water and dry it slowly with a clean towel.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 17, 'Set a timer for two minutes and step away from your desk, screen or chores until it rings.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 18, 'Sit near someone you live with, even without talking, for ten minutes this evening.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 19, 'Wrap up in your coziest blanket for a few minutes, wherever you are sitting.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 20, 'Make tonight''s dinner the simplest thing you can manage: toast, cereal, a frozen meal. It still counts as dinner.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 21, 'Pet an animal for a few minutes, yours or a friendly neighbor''s, and let your shoulders drop.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 22, 'Lower one expectation for today on purpose, and name it: "The dishes can wait until tomorrow."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 23, 'Put on a familiar show you have seen many times and let it play in the background.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 24, 'Roll your shoulders back five times, slowly, then let your jaw hang loose for a moment.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 25, 'Write a short, honest message to your manager or teacher: "Today is a tough one. Can this wait until tomorrow?"'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 26, 'Go to bed early tonight, even thirty minutes earlier than usual, without finishing everything first.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 27, 'Before bed, jot one line about what helped even a little today, so you can find it on the next hard day.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 28, 'Ask one person for one concrete favor today, like picking up milk or making one phone call for you.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 29, 'Say no to one thing today that you do not have room for, kindly and briefly.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 30, 'Take a warm shower and let the water run over the back of your neck for a full minute.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 31, 'Open a window or stand by an open door and take five slow breaths of fresh air.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 32, 'Find one comfort food you can have today without any cooking, and enjoy it slowly.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 33, 'Turn off notifications on your phone for one hour, so the day stops tapping you on the shoulder.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 34, 'Look at your to-do list and cross off one thing that does not truly need doing at all.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 35, 'Put both hands on your chest, feel it rise and fall, and count five breaths.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 36, 'Walk around the block once, slowly, with no goal other than getting some air.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 37, 'Tell yourself, "I only have to get through the next ten minutes," and then do just that.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 38, 'Choose one tiny thing to finish, like replying to one email or folding one towel, and let that be a win.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 39, 'Sit in your parked car for five minutes before you go inside, and breathe before the next part of the day.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 40, 'Give the kids an extra hour of screen time today without guilt, and use that hour to rest.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 41, 'Notice where you are holding tension right now, in your hands, jaw or stomach, and loosen it a little.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 42, 'On a dark winter afternoon, turn on a warm lamp early and make one corner of the room feel bright.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 43, 'Call someone you trust and say, "Can you just talk to me about anything for a few minutes?"'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 44, 'Let yourself cry if tears come, somewhere private, and then drink some water after.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 45, 'Stretch your arms over your head as high as they will go, hold for a breath, and let them fall.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 46, 'Write down the worst part of today in one sentence, then fold the paper and put it away.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 47, 'Hum or sing one verse of a song you have known since you were young.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 48, 'When the afternoon slump hits, step away for a glass of water and a small snack before you push on.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 49, 'Remind yourself, "I do not have to do this perfectly. I just have to do it, or let it wait."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 50, 'Eat lunch away from your desk or work area today, even if it is only for ten minutes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 51, 'Make a cup of tea, coffee or warm water, and hold the mug in both hands while it cools.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 52, 'If you cannot sleep tonight, get up for a few minutes, sit somewhere dim and quiet, and go back when you feel drowsy.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 53, 'Put your phone in another room for twenty minutes and notice the quiet it leaves behind.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 54, 'Name one small thing that went okay today, even if it was only that you ate breakfast.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 55, 'Ask for help with one caregiving task today, even something as small as a bath time or a school pickup.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 56, 'Brush your teeth and comb your hair, even late in the day, and notice how a small reset feels.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 57, 'Look out a window for one minute and find three things that are moving: a tree, a cloud, a car.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 58, 'Pick one chore you can skip entirely today without anything bad happening, and skip it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 59, 'Send a short note to a teacher asking for a little extra time on one assignment, and keep it simple.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 60, 'Spend ten minutes doing something with your hands that asks nothing of you, like doodling or sorting socks.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 61, 'In summer heat, run cool water over your wrists and the back of your neck, then sit in the shade for a while.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 62, 'Close your eyes and picture a place where you have felt safe, and stay there in your mind for one minute.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 63, 'Let one call go to voicemail today, and return it when you have a little more in you.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 64, 'Tidy one small surface, like your nightstand or the corner of a table, and stop there.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 65, 'Remember a hard day you already got through, and remind yourself that you got through that one too.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 66, 'Tell the people at home, "I''m running low today," so they know what kind of day it is.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 67, 'Put on warm socks or slippers, and take a moment to notice your feet feeling looked after.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 68, 'Turn off the news for the rest of today and choose something lighter to fill the silence.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 69, 'If the day feels like too much, text or call someone you trust right now, or reach 988 any time by call or text.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 70, 'Let tomorrow be a new day, and say so out loud before you turn off the light tonight.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 71, 'Get some daylight on your face for five minutes, through a window or out on a step.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 72, 'Write a three-line list of what can wait until next week, and feel how much lighter today gets.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 73, 'Pour yourself a glass of something cold and drink it slowly, sitting down.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 74, 'Set the alarm for the next part of your day, then rest your eyes for ten minutes before it goes off.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 75, 'Split the next task into the smallest first step, like "open the document," and do only that step.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 76, 'Choose a phrase to carry today, such as "One thing at a time," and write it on your hand or a sticky note.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 77, 'Grab a piece of cheese, a boiled egg or a spoonful of peanut butter if you have been running on empty.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 78, 'Message a friend just to say, "Thinking of you. Rough day here, how is yours?"'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 79, 'Stand in the sun for a few minutes, close your eyes and feel the warmth on your face.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 80, 'Decide on one thing you can postpone until tomorrow, and move it right now so it stops nagging.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 81, 'Put on the most comfortable clothes you own, and let your body know the hard part can ease.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 82, 'Make a short playlist of three songs that lift you, and play it on your way to the next thing.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 83, 'Ask, "What is the least I can do here and still be okay?" Then do that version.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 84, 'Rest your head on your arms at your desk or table for two minutes, eyes closed.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 85, 'Breathe in through your nose for a count of four and out for six, five times, wherever you are.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 86, 'Cancel one optional plan tonight with a short, kind message, and let that evening be yours.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 87, 'Give yourself the same patience you would give a coworker who was clearly having a bad day.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 88, 'Splash cold water on your hands and face when you feel overheated or overwhelmed.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 89, 'Leave your workspace for a two-minute walk to the end of the hall, the kitchen or the door and back.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 90, 'Sit on the couch next to someone you love tonight, and let that be enough company.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 91, 'Pull a heavy blanket over your lap and let the weight settle you for a few minutes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 92, 'Order or pick up a simple dinner tonight if cooking feels like one thing too many.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 93, 'Look at photos of a trip, a friend or a happy time for a few minutes, and let them warm you.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 94, 'Drop the bar for tonight: a quick rinse instead of a full clean, a sandwich instead of a meal.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 95, 'Watch one episode of a comforting show, and give yourself full permission to enjoy it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 96, 'Gently turn your head side to side, chin toward each shoulder, three times each way.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 97, 'Reply to the most pressing email with three honest lines and a promise to follow up later.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 98, 'Turn the lights down early tonight and let your body know the day is winding toward its end.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 99, 'Write a short note to future you about what made today hard and what got you through it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 100, 'Ask someone at home to handle one task tonight, and say exactly which one.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 101, 'Turn down one request today with "I can''t take that on right now," and leave it there.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 102, 'Run a warm bath or a shower and stay in a few minutes longer than you need to.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 103, 'Crack a window in your room or car and breathe the outside air for a minute.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 104, 'Eat a meal that reminds you of being looked after, even if it comes out of a can.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 105, 'Silence group chats for the afternoon, and check them later when you have more room.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 106, 'Hand off or share one item on your list with someone who can take it today.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 107, 'Lay one hand on your stomach and feel it move with three slow breaths.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 108, 'Walk to the mailbox, the corner or the end of the driveway, and notice the air on the way.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 109, 'Tell yourself, "I can do hard things slowly," and slow down the next thing you do.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 110, 'Do one two-minute task you have been putting off, then stop and let it count.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 111, 'Park somewhere quiet for a few minutes before you head home, and let the music play.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 112, 'Serve the easiest family dinner you can think of tonight, like pasta with butter, and call it a win.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 113, 'Unclench your fists, open your hands on your lap, and leave them open for a few breaths.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 114, 'On a dark evening, light a candle or a warm lamp before you start on anything else.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 115, 'Phone a relative or old friend just to hear a familiar voice for a few minutes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 116, 'Write the word "enough" on a sticky note and put it where you will see it when you feel the urge to do more.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 117, 'Reach your arms out wide, like you are taking up the whole room, and hold for three breaths.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 118, 'Write the hardest thing about today at the top of a page, then write one thing you can do about it below.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 119, 'Sing along to one song in the car or the shower, as loudly as you like.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 120, 'Take a short break in the midafternoon, even five minutes, before the slump gets heavier.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 121, 'Remind yourself that doing the minimum today is still doing something.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 122, 'Step away from the screen at lunch and eat somewhere you can see a window or the sky.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 123, 'Warm your hands around a hot drink, and take three slow sips before you go on.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 124, 'If you are awake in the middle of the night, put on a soft, boring podcast and let your mind drift with it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 125, 'Leave your phone charging in the kitchen for the evening, and pick it up only when you choose to.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 126, 'Find one thing that went a little better than expected today, and let yourself notice it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 127, 'Tell a partner, friend or family member, "I need an hour to myself," and take it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 128, 'Put on a fresh pair of socks or a clean shirt in the middle of the day, just for the reset.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 129, 'Watch the light change outside for a minute, without needing to do anything with it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 130, 'Let the laundry, the dishes or the inbox wait one more day, and choose rest instead.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 131, 'Ask your teacher or professor for a short extension in one plain, polite sentence.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 132, 'Color, scribble or doodle on any paper for five minutes, with no aim at all.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 133, 'On a hot day, put a cool, damp cloth on your forehead and lie down for a few minutes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 134, 'Picture the end of today, when you are in bed and it is over, and remember that moment is coming.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 135, 'Set an away message or status that says you will reply tomorrow, and let it do the explaining.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 136, 'Clear one small space, like the seat of a chair, so you have somewhere to sit and breathe.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 137, 'Write down three people you could text on a hard day, and keep the list in your phone.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 138, 'Ask the people around you for a little extra quiet this evening, and tell them it is not about them.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 139, 'Wear something that feels warm and soft, like a sweater you love, for the rest of the day.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 140, 'Choose a gentle podcast or audiobook for the trip home instead of the news.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 141, 'Reach out to someone you trust right now if today feels too heavy to hold alone. You can also call or text 988 any time.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 142, 'Sit on the floor with your back against the couch and let yourself be still for five minutes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 143, 'Rinse your hands under warm water for thirty seconds and let the warmth slow you down.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 144, 'Unplug from work email after dinner tonight, and let the morning handle it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 145, 'Sip a glass of water slowly, all the way to the bottom, before your next task.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 146, 'Keep a glass of water by your bed tonight, so the morning starts with one easy thing already done.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 147, 'Wake up and, before you check your phone, sit on the edge of the bed and take three slow breaths.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 148, 'Skip the full morning routine if you need to, and do only the two parts that make you feel human.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 149, 'Eat breakfast even if it is tiny, like a banana in the car or toast standing at the counter.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 150, 'Tell one coworker you trust, "I''m a little off today," so you do not have to pretend all day.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 151, 'Close the door, or put on headphones, for fifteen minutes of fewer interruptions at work.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 152, 'Write tomorrow''s first task on a sticky note before you leave work, so you can stop thinking about it tonight.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 153, 'Break one big school assignment into three tiny pieces, and only start the first piece today.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 154, 'Message your manager to ask which two things matter most today, and let the rest slide down the list.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 155, 'Use one break between classes or meetings to sit still, breathe, and drink some water.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 156, 'Put a familiar movie on for the kids tonight, settle in beside them, and rest while it plays.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 157, 'Make a simple snack plate for dinner: crackers, cheese, fruit, whatever is in the fridge.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 158, 'Ask another parent, a neighbor or a relative to cover one pickup or drop-off this week.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 159, 'Take five minutes alone in the bathroom or a quiet room if caregiving has you stretched thin.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 160, 'Say "yes" the next time someone offers to help, and let them do it their way.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 161, 'Give yourself one easy evening after a hard day: nothing scheduled, nothing to prove.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 162, 'Lay out tomorrow''s clothes tonight, so the morning asks one less thing of you.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 163, 'Let tonight''s dinner come from the freezer, and do not apologize to anyone for it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 164, 'Spend the last half hour before bed with no screens, just a dim light and something soft to read.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 165, 'On the morning after a rough day, remind yourself, "Today gets to be its own day."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 166, 'Look back over this challenge so far and notice which small things helped you most.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 167, 'During holiday season, choose one tradition to skip or simplify this year, and let it go without guilt.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 168, 'Leave a gathering a little early if you are running low, with a warm "Thank you, I need to head home."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 169, 'When family pressure builds over the holidays, step outside for five minutes of cold air and quiet.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 170, 'Keep a cool drink close by on a hot afternoon, and sip it every time you finish a small task.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 171, 'In the heat of summer, do the hardest errand early, while the air is still cool, and rest later.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 172, 'On a gray winter morning, open every curtain in the house and let in whatever light there is.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 173, 'Bundle up and stand outside for five minutes on a cold day, then come in and warm your hands.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 174, 'If your thoughts turn toward harming yourself, you are not alone. Call or text 988, the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline, any time, or call 911 in an emergency.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 175, 'Find the person you feel safest with and stay near them for a while, even if you say very little.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 176, 'Text a friend a simple ask: "Could you check on me tonight?"'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 177, 'Say to yourself, "I''m doing the best I can with what I have today," and mean it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 178, 'Remind yourself that a slow, messy day is still a day you got through.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 179, 'Imagine a good friend sitting beside you right now. Notice what kind words they would say.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 180, 'Forgive yourself, out loud, for one thing you did not get done today.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 181, 'Let "good enough" be the goal for every task left on today''s list.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 182, 'Write down one kind sentence about yourself, as if a friend wrote it for you.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 183, 'Listen to a song that matches how you feel, then one that feels a little lighter.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 184, 'Rewatch a funny clip that always makes you smile, even if only a little.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 185, 'Curl up somewhere soft and read a few pages of something easy and familiar.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 186, 'Heat up soup or another warm meal, and eat it slowly at a table if you can.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 187, 'Take a ten-minute walk after dinner, even just up and down your street.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 188, 'Sit in a sunny spot indoors, like a patch of light on the floor, for a few minutes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 189, 'Lie on your back with your legs up against a wall for five minutes and let your breathing slow.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 190, 'Rub your temples or the back of your neck gently for one minute.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 191, 'Shake out your hands and arms for twenty seconds, then let them hang still.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 192, 'Shower in the evening, and imagine some of the day going down the drain with the water.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 193, 'Change your sheets or just your pillowcase tonight, so bed feels fresh when you get there.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 194, 'Drink a glass of water first thing when you get home, before anything else.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 195, 'Snack on something crunchy, like an apple or a few nuts, when the afternoon starts to drag.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 196, 'Ask a friend if you can sit together at a coffee shop or library, each doing your own thing.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 197, 'Call a family member and ask them to tell you about their day instead of talking about yours.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 198, 'Text a funny picture or a silly memory to someone who will understand, just to share a moment.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 199, 'Let someone you trust know you might need a check-in later, and give them a time.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 200, 'Sit in the same room as your pet and let their calm be the calmest thing in the room.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 201, 'Sit in a parked car or on a quiet bench with a favorite song for a few minutes before you go back to people.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 202, 'Choose the next small thing, and let everything after it stay blurry for now.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 203, 'Circle the one task that will make tomorrow easier, and do only that tonight.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 204, 'Push one deadline you set for yourself back by a day, and notice the relief.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 205, 'Shorten one meeting or call today by five minutes, and use those minutes to breathe.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 206, 'Delete or snooze three items from your to-do list that you added just to feel busy.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 207, 'Take one item off your plate by asking, "Could you take care of this one for me?"'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 208, 'Keep your evening plans to one thing only, and let that be plenty.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 209, 'Prepare a hot water bottle or a warm pack for your lap or feet on a chilly night.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 210, 'Let a quiet room, a closed door and five minutes of stillness be your break.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 211, 'Notice one sound you like right now, a fan, a bird, the fridge humming, and listen for a moment.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 212, 'Hold something warm, like a mug or a warm towel, and let the heat soak into your hands.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 213, 'Pick a soft, cheerful color to wear or carry today, a scarf, a pen, a mug.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 214, 'Go to sleep tonight knowing you did enough, even if the list still has things on it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 215, 'Turn the thermostat or the fan to whatever feels most comfortable, and let your body rest in it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 216, 'On a sleepless night, write down whatever is looping in your head, then close the notebook and rest your eyes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 217, 'Ask yourself, "What do I need right now: food, rest, quiet or company?" and give yourself one of them.'),
