  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 220, 'Refill your water bottle and keep it within reach for the rest of the afternoon.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 221, 'Pack tomorrow''s lunch tonight, or decide you will buy it, so the morning has one less decision.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 222, 'Swap one long task for its shortest version today, like a quick reply instead of a full report.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 223, 'Stand up, reach for the ceiling, then bend and let your arms dangle toward the floor for a few breaths.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 224, 'Sit outside on a bench, step or stoop for ten minutes, and watch the world go by.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 225, 'Tell yourself out loud, "I''m allowed to have a bad day."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 226, 'Text someone you trust one honest word about how you feel, and let that be the whole message.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 227, 'Find a quiet corner at school or work, and spend three minutes there with your eyes closed.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 228, 'Reheat leftovers for dinner tonight, and count that as cooking.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 229, 'Let the kids pick an easy dinner tonight, like breakfast for supper, and call it fun instead of failing.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 230, 'Ask your partner or a friend to watch the kids for thirty minutes so you can rest.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 231, 'Trade one caregiving task with someone else in the family for today.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 232, 'Plan a slow, quiet evening tonight with one thing to look forward to, like a warm drink or a favorite show.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 233, 'Note one thing that made today a little easier, and keep the note where you will find it next time.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 234, 'Wake gently tomorrow by giving yourself five extra minutes in bed before you get up.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 235, 'Imagine putting today''s worries in a box on a high shelf for the night, and close the lid.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 236, 'Go to bed with a warm drink and the lights low, and let the day end there.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 237, 'Breathe in the smell of something comforting, like coffee, soap or a lemon peel, and take your time.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 238, 'Clench your hands tight for five seconds, then release them, and feel the difference.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 239, 'Sit with your feet flat on the floor and your back supported, and let the chair hold you for a minute.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 240, 'Turn on a fan or open a window if the room feels stuffy, and let the air move around you.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 241, 'Step into the shade, a cool lobby or an air-conditioned store for a few minutes on a hot day.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 242, 'On a short winter day, go for a walk in the early afternoon while the light is still out.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 243, 'Plan one small, warm treat for a dark evening, like a bath, cocoa or a favorite blanket.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 244, 'Ask a family member to share one holiday job with you this year, like cooking or wrapping.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 245, 'Choose a simple, store-bought dish to bring to a holiday gathering, and let that be your contribution.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 246, 'Allow yourself to celebrate the season in a quieter way this year, if that is what you have room for.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 247, 'Call or text 988 if a hard day starts to feel unbearable or unsafe. Someone will answer any time, and in an emergency, call 911.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 248, 'Wrap a scarf or a sweater around your shoulders and take a moment to feel looked after.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 249, 'Ask a friend to send you a voice message about anything, so you can hear a kind voice.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 250, 'Write a short text to someone you have not talked to in a while, and say, "I was thinking of you."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 251, 'Spend a few minutes in a busy, friendly place, like a café or a park, just being among people.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 252, 'Let a friend know you need company, not advice: "Can we just hang out for a bit?"'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 253, 'Remember that a hard day does not mean you are doing life wrong.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 254, 'Be as gentle with yourself as you would be with a tired child.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 255, 'Speak to yourself in a kind tone for the next hour, the way you would talk to a friend.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 256, 'Lower the bar on one task to "done, not perfect," and then finish it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 257, 'Thank yourself for one thing you managed today, however small.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 258, 'Play the album you loved when you were a teenager, and let it carry you for a while.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 259, 'Rewatch a favorite movie, and let the familiar parts do the comforting.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 260, 'Make your bed with an extra pillow or blanket tonight so it feels like a nest.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 261, 'Treat yourself to one small, comforting thing you can buy for a few dollars, like a favorite snack.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 262, 'Walk somewhere green, a park, a tree-lined street, a garden, for ten minutes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 263, 'Spend ten minutes outside after dark, looking at the stars, the moon or the city lights.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 264, 'Drink a glass of water with a slice of lemon or a splash of juice, just to make it nicer.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 265, 'Have a small snack with protein, like yogurt or nuts, if you feel shaky or foggy.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 266, 'Brush out your hair slowly, or wash it, and notice the small care in it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 267, 'Rest on the couch for twenty minutes with your feet up and nothing in your hands.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 268, 'Lie down on your side, pull your knees up a little, and breathe slowly for a few minutes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 269, 'Pick one muscle that feels tight, maybe your shoulders or your back, and stretch it gently for a minute.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 270, 'Choose one task to stop for today, and say to yourself, "That''s enough for now."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 271, 'Agree with yourself that the next hour has only one job, and let everything else sit outside it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 272, 'Pause before saying yes to anything new today, and give yourself until tomorrow to answer.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 273, 'Ask for one small change at work today, like moving a meeting or sharing a task.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 274, 'Email your teacher or professor to say you are having a hard time and ask what flexibility there is.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 275, 'Take a five-minute break every hour this afternoon, even just to stand and look out a window.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 276, 'Leave work on time today, even if the inbox is not empty.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 277, 'Put a hand on your heart and say, "This is hard, and I''m still here."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 278, 'Accept that some things will be messy today, and let them be messy.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 279, 'Check in with your body: hungry, thirsty, tired or cold? Fix just one of those.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 280, 'Plan a short call with someone you trust for later today, so you have something steady to look toward.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 281, 'Wave to a neighbor, chat with a cashier, or say hello to someone you pass, just for a moment of connection.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 282, 'Hug someone you trust, or a pillow, for a full ten seconds.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 283, 'Sit close to a pet and match your breathing to theirs for a minute.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 284, 'Let your child or a family member pick a game or story tonight, and simply enjoy being together.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 285, 'Bring something small and comforting to work or school, a photo, a smooth stone, a soft sweater.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 286, 'Plan tomorrow''s easy wins tonight: one meal, one task, one kind thing for yourself.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 287, 'When the day ends, say to yourself, "It''s over. I made it through."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 288, 'If you wake in the night and cannot settle, turn on a soft light, read something gentle, and let sleep find you again.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 289, 'Get up a few minutes early tomorrow to sit quietly with a warm drink before the day begins.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 290, 'Say goodnight to the hard parts of today by naming them once, quietly, and then turning out the light.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 291, 'Leave the kitchen as it is tonight if cleaning it would cost the last of your energy.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 292, 'Keep your evening simple tonight: dinner, a shower, bed.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 293, 'Pause in the doorway before you walk into the next room or meeting, and let one long breath out.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 294, 'Put a snack in your bag or pocket today, so hunger cannot sneak up on you during a long stretch.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 295, 'Fill a big glass of water and set it where you will see it, then drink it before lunch.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 296, 'Wear something today that makes you feel a little more like yourself, even just a favorite ring or hat.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 297, 'Take off your shoes when you get home, stretch your toes, and let your feet rest on the cool floor.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 298, 'Stretch your back gently, hands on your lower back, leaning a little backward, and breathe.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 299, 'Roll a tennis ball or water bottle under your foot for a minute while you sit.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 300, 'Doze for twenty minutes this afternoon if you can, with an alarm set so you can let go.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 301, 'Step outside on your lunch break, even if it is only to the sidewalk or the parking lot.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 302, 'Notice the sky once in the morning and once in the evening today, and see how it changed.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 303, 'Cross one thing off your list that someone else is waiting on, then let the rest wait.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 304, 'Write down everything on your mind, then circle the one thing that has to happen today.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 305, 'Choose a single focus for the afternoon and close every tab, window and app that is not it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 306, 'Give one task half the effort today and see if it still turns out fine.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 307, 'Turn one "should" for today into a "could," and decide later if you will.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 308, 'Reschedule one appointment that can wait, and feel the space it opens up.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 309, 'Let someone else make one decision for you today, like what to eat or what to watch.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 310, 'Admit to yourself that today is too full, and pick the one thing that matters most in it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 311, 'Send a one-line message to a trusted friend: "Rough day. Could use a kind word."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 312, 'Ask the person nearest you for one small kindness, like a cup of tea or a quiet half hour.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 313, 'Call a friend while you walk, so you get fresh air and a familiar voice at the same time.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 314, 'Share a meal or a snack with someone today, even if you barely talk.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 315, 'Find someone who makes you laugh, and spend a few minutes with them or with their messages.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 316, 'Ask a friend to tell you one good thing from their week, and just enjoy hearing it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 317, 'Offer yourself the words, "It makes sense that this is hard."'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 318, 'Remind yourself that being tired is not the same as failing.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 319, 'Picture yourself on a calmer day, and send that version of you a kind thought.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 320, 'Let one mistake today be just a mistake, and move on to the next small thing.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 321, 'Ask yourself, "Will this matter a month from now?" and, if not, let it go a little.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 322, 'Tell yourself, "I can come back to this later," and set it down for now.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 323, 'Make a cup of cocoa, warm milk or herbal tea, and drink it before bed.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 324, 'Pull on your coziest sweatshirt or hoodie, and let it be your armor for the rest of the day.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 325, 'Play a gentle instrumental playlist while you work through the next hour.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 326, 'Read a chapter of a book you have loved before, and let the familiar story hold you.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 327, 'Watch a show from your childhood, or one that feels like home, for twenty minutes.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 328, 'Cook one simple comfort dish tonight, like eggs on toast or a bowl of rice, and eat it warm.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 329, 'Stroll slowly around your home or office for five minutes, just to change your view.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 330, 'Notice when your energy is lowest today, and plan only easy tasks for that time.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 331, 'Let a coworker know in one honest line: "I''m running behind today. Can we push this to tomorrow?"'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 332, 'Close your laptop or put down your books for five minutes, and look at something far away.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 333, 'Ask a classmate to share notes from one class, so you can catch up without stress.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 334, 'Work in a different spot for an hour today, like a library, a café or another room.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 335, 'Let a family member or friend take the kids to the park so you can have one quiet hour.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 336, 'Serve a "picnic dinner" on the floor tonight, with whatever is easy, and let it be fun.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 337, 'Let go of a perfect bedtime routine for the kids tonight, and keep only the cuddle or the story.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 338, 'Tell the person you care for, gently, that you need a short break, and take it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 339, 'Call a friend or relative and ask, "Could you sit with Mom for an hour this week?"'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 340, 'Put a note by your bed with one thing to look forward to tomorrow, however small.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 341, 'Write one sentence about how you got through today, so you remember you can.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 342, 'Tell yourself before bed, "Tomorrow can be easier," and let the night do its work.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 343, 'Thank a friend the morning after a hard day if they helped, even in a small way.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 344, 'Remember that you do not have to fix everything tonight. Sleep is allowed first.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 345, 'Rest your hand on a warm cup or a pet, and breathe slowly as you go to sleep.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 346, 'On a summer evening, sit out on a porch, balcony or step after the heat breaks, and enjoy the cooler air.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 347, 'During a winter cold snap, run a warm shower, put on thick socks and get under a blanket early.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 348, 'Plan one small thing to look forward to during a hard week, like a favorite meal or a phone call.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 349, 'Give yourself permission to say "not this year" to one holiday expectation that weighs on you.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 350, 'Look for a few quiet minutes during a busy holiday, like a short walk or time alone with a coffee.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 351, 'Talk to someone you trust right now if you feel you cannot get through today. You can call or text 988 any time, and if you are in danger, call 911.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 352, 'Remember that 988 is there for hard nights too: you can call or text it any time you need to talk to someone.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 353, 'Choose a comfortable spot to sit, and let your shoulders sink a little lower with each out breath.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 354, 'Rub a little lotion into your hands slowly, and let it be a minute of care.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 355, 'Stand by an open window at night, breathe the cool air, and watch the quiet street for a minute.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 356, 'Spend a few minutes tidying your bag or backpack, so tomorrow starts a little lighter.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 357, 'Turn on a soft light and some quiet music while you do one small evening chore.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 358, 'Buy or pick a few flowers, or a single green leaf, and put it somewhere you will see it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 359, 'Put away anything on your desk or table that reminds you of today''s stress, until tomorrow.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 360, 'Make a short "hard day kit" list: one song, one snack, one person, one place, for next time.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 361, 'Ask yourself what the smallest helpful thing would be right now, and do it.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 362, 'Allow yourself to do nothing for fifteen minutes, and call it rest instead of wasting time.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 363, 'Choose one thing that feels calming, like folding laundry or watering a plant, and do it slowly.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 364, 'Settle into bed a few minutes early tonight, and let the quiet be the last thing of the day.'),
  ('getting-through-a-hard-day', 365, 'Look in the mirror and say, "You''re doing okay," even if it feels a little silly.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
join public.challenge_templates t on t.slug = v.slug;
